"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nIn the final scene, Yukiho's last appearance, not batting an eye, conveys both shock and sadness.  \nIt would be an expression of her cruelty and a final struggle to hide the sadness of losing her only sun.  \nIt must be a famous scene that is  yet desperately beautiful.  \n\nTheir relationship is too bizarre and desperate to be called love, and it deeply explores the complex and dark abyss of human existence beyond a simple distinction between good and evil.  \n\nThe psychology of the protagonists in the work is not directly narrated, so one must follow the story carefully.  \n\nIn fact, it's difficult to fully empathize with their story and actions.  \n\nIt leaves a deep lingering impression that makes the heart ache for a long time.  "